===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|h₂epó}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-}}
{{lbor|en|LL.|abligūrītiōnem}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ion|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|noun}}s denoting actions or processes, or their results}}. {{m|la||Abligūrītiōnem}} is the {{glossary|accusative}} {{glossary|singular}} of {{m|LL.|abliguritiō}}, {{m|LL.|abligurrītiō|t=act of devouring; act of spending in feasting}}, from {{der|en|la|abligurrītus|t=(having been) squandered or wasted}} + {{m|la|-iō|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|abstract noun}}s from {{glossary|verb}}s}}; while {{m|la|abligurrītus}} is the {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|abligurriō|t=to lick away; (''figuratively'') to spend or waste indulgently, squander}}, from {{m|la|ab-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘away; away from; from’}} + {{m|la|ligurriō}}, {{m|la|liguriō|t=to lick up; to feast or feed upon; to be dainty or fond of luxuries}} (from {{m|la|lingō|t=to lick (up)}} (from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-|t=to lick}}) + probably {{m|la|-uriō|pos=suffix meaning ‘to desire or wish’}}).<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|entry=† abligurition|pos=n|id=396|date=June 2021}}</ref>

